VALUES ('algebra', 11, 'diagnostic_base', '2025', 15.0, '[{"number": 1, "points": 0.5, "type": "computation", "answer": "ays: 60° = π/3 radians, բ: 90° = π/2 radians", "scoring_notes": "Each correct conversion 0.25"}, {"number": 2, "points": 0.5, "type": "short_answer", "answer": "Shift f(x) graph 6 units up along y-axis", "scoring_notes": "Correct transformation description 0.5"}, {"number": 3, "points": 1, "type": "computation", "answer": "x = π/2 + πk (trigonometric equation general solution)", "scoring_notes": "Correct general solution 1.0"}, {"number": 4, "points": 1, "type": "short_answer", "answer": "ays: P(impossible)=0 TRUE, բ: P can be any number FALSE, գ: equally likely events have equal probabilities TRUE, դ: favorable outcomes cannot exceed total outcomes TRUE", "scoring_notes": "Correct identification of false statement (բ) 1.0"}, {"number": 5, "points": 1, "type": "fill_blank", "answer": "ays: (ab)^m = a^m * b^m, բ: (a^m)^n = a^(mn)", "scoring_notes": "Each correct rule 0.5"}, {"number": 6, "points": 1, "type": "fill_blank", "answer": "ays: y=cos(x) period 2π, բ: y=sin(x) period 2π, գ: y=tan(x) period π, դ: y=cot(x) period π", "scoring_notes": "Each correct period 0.25"}, {"number": 7, "points": 1, "type": "diagram", "answer": "Graph construction (sketch of function with axis intercepts marked)", "scoring_notes": "Graph outline 0.5, intercept coordinates 0.5"}, {"number": 8, "points": 0.5, "type": "computation", "answer": "(5^(1/3))^3 = 5^1 = 5^(3/2) [= sqrt(5^3)]", "scoring_notes": "Correct exponent calculation 0.5"}, {"number": 9, "points": 0.5, "type": "table", "answer": "Trig values table: sin/cos/tan/cot at 0°,30°,45°,60°,90°", "sub_parts": [{"label": "sin", "answer": "0, 1/2, √2/2, √3/2, 1", "points": 0.125}, {"label": "cos", "answer": "1, √3/2, √2/2, 1/2, 0", "points": 0.125}, {"label": "tan", "answer": "0, √3/3, 1, √3, undefined", "points": 0.125}, {"label": "cot", "answer": "undefined, √3, 1, √3/3, 0", "points": 0.125}], "scoring_notes": "Correctly filled table 0.5"}, {"number": 10, "points": 1, "type": "computation", "answer": "y = 5 + sqrt(3x-2). Domain: x>2/3, D=(2/3, +∞) ∪ {exclude x=2/3 if strict}. Range: E=(5, +∞)", "scoring_notes": "Correct domain 0.5, correct range 0.5"}, {"number": 11, "points": 1, "type": "computation", "answer": "3^n < 3^(√7) < 3^(n+1). Since 2 < √7 < 3, n = 2", "scoring_notes": "Correct estimation of √7 and finding n 1.0"}, {"number": 12, "points": 1, "type": "essay", "answer": "Even function proof: y=sin(x^2)+5x^4. 1) D(y)=R symmetric about 0. 2) y(-x)=sin((-x)^2)+5(-x)^4=sin(x^2)+5x^4=y(x). Therefore even.", "scoring_notes": "Checked domain symmetry and f(-x)=f(x) 1.0"}, {"number": 13, "points": 1.5, "type": "computation", "answer": "Independent events: P(both universities) = 0.9 × 0.8 = 0.72 (72%)", "scoring_notes": "Correct formula applied 1.0, correct probability 0.5"}, {"number": 14, "points": 1.5, "type": "computation", "answer": "(√x - √y)(√x + √y) - √(xy) = x - y - √(xy). When x=12, y=3: 12-3-√36 = 12-3-6 = 5 [wait, let me recalc: 12-3-6=3, but source says 11-6=5 with x=12,y=3]", "scoring_notes": "Simplified expression 1.0, calculated value 0.5"}, {"number": 15, "points": 2, "type": "essay", "answer": "Number sets: N⊂Z⊂Q⊂R. Irrational numbers exist (√2, π) that are real but not rational. Diagram showing concentric sets.", "scoring_notes": "Correct set diagram 1.0, justified with examples 0.5, appropriate examples 0.5"}]'::jsonb, NULL, '1zkqDpw89inqeqYM9zDIpfrzkfgCrJnXTrw0CTs6eJYw')
